WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.460
Hello, welcome to another Friday Chit Chat.
大家好，欢迎来到又一期的周五闲聊。

2
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.720
Hi, we have a fun little guest in the studio with us.
嗨，我们今天的工作室里来了一位有趣的小嘉宾。

3
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.500
So we have Sam, we have Cassie,
我们有萨姆，有卡西，

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.660
and then we have Colin who worked with us at Earwolf.
还有曾在 Earwolf 和我们一起工作的科林。

5
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:13.560
Colin, say hi.
科林，打个招呼吧。

6
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.140
Hey.
嘿。

7
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.720
Colin's visiting and we have forced him to come in the studio
科林来串门，我们强行把他拉进了工作室

8
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.220
and be on mic with you today.
今天陪你们一起用麦克风聊聊天。

9
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.660
Yeah, I hate being on microphone.
对，我讨厌用麦克风。

10
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.620
I like listening to podcasts, watching podcasts,
我喜欢听播客，看播客，

11
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.200
not talking on podcasts.
而不是在播客里说话。

12
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.760
You're going to do just fine.
你会表现得很棒的。

13
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:27.340
Great.
太好了。

14
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.560
Angela, you said you have a share.
安吉拉，你说你有东西要分享。

15
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:30.500
Well, I do.
对，我是有。

16
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:35.580
Okay, so a while back, there was an article in The New Yorker,
好啦，不久前，《纽约客》上有一篇文章，

17
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.120
and it was called, Why Do We Still Love The Office?
它的标题是：《为什么我们依然热爱〈办公室〉？》

18
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.760
And it had an illustration for the article.
这篇文章还配有一幅插图。

19
00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.400
It's of everyone in the bullpen.
画的是大办公室里的所有人。

20
00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.740
And Jenna, I loved it because right front and center
珍娜，我很喜欢它，因为正前方正中央

21
00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.080
are Pam and Angela.
就是帕姆和安吉拉。

22
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.900
Angela even has one of her cats.
安吉拉甚至还带着她的一只猫。

23
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.660
I'm going to put this in our stories.
我一会儿把它发到我们的快拍里。

24
00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:53.440
Do you see that?
你看到了吗？

25
00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:54.560
Yes.
看到了。

26
00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:55.220
Okay.
好。

27
00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.440
Well, I just kind of became obsessed with it because,
总之，我有点对它着迷了，因为，

28
00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.420
I mean, our two characters are the front two characters,
我是说，我们两个角色成了最前方的两个角色，

29
00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:06.060
and that so rarely happens for us in any kind of artwork
这在任何为《办公室》创作的艺术作品中

30
00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.600
that's done for the office.
对我们来说都是极其罕见的。

31
00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:12.540
So I found the artist, and his name is Max Dalton,
所以我找到了这位艺术家，他叫马克斯·道尔顿，

32
00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.740
and he does a lot of illustrations.
他创作了大量插画。

33
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.280
And I DM'd him on Instagram, and I said,
我在 Instagram 上给他发了私信，我说，

34
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.380
is there any way I can get a copy of this drawing?
我有没有什么办法能弄到一张这幅画的复制品？

35
00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:22.800
I love it so much.
我太喜欢它了。

36
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.700
And he was like, absolutely.
然后他说，当然可以。

37
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.800
And he sent me this note.
他还给我寄了这张便条。

38
00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.220
He said,
他说，

39
00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.420
Dear Angela,
亲爱的安吉拉，

40
00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.720
here's two copies of my illustration of the office,
这是两份我画的《办公室》插画复制品，

41
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.720
because I asked if I could have one for you, too.
因为我问过是否也能为你留一份。

42
00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:35.820
Stop it.
别开玩笑了。

43
00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:36.720
And he said,
接着他说，

44
00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:37.860
as you know,
如你所知，

45
00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:41.360
the illustration was made only for an article in The New Yorker,
这幅插画只是为《纽约客》的一篇文章创作的，

46
00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.640
so it's unfortunately quite small.
所以遗憾的是它非常小。

47
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:44.920
And then he put in parentheses,
然后他在括号里写道，

48
00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.520
woulda that's what she said apply here?
“这算不算‘她说的’这句话适用的时候呢？”

49
00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.600
And then he wrote on to say,
接着他又写道，

50
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.100
I hope that's not too disappointing.
希望这不会太令人失望。

51
00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.420
Thanks to you and Jenna and the rest of the cast
谢谢你、珍娜以及剧组的其他成员

52
00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:54.960
for all the hilarious moments.
带给我们所有欢乐的时刻。

53
00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.200
Love, Max.
爱你的，马克斯。

54
00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:58.600
Oh, my gosh.
噢，我的天哪。

55
00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.160
Yes.
是的。

56
00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.420
And now you and I each have one.
现在你和我各有一个了。

57
00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.580
I love that lady.
我太喜欢这位女士了。

58
00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:04.880
That is so sweet.
这太贴心了。

59
00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:06.340
It's so beautiful.
它太美了。

60
00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:07.580
I love his drawing.
我很喜欢他的画。

61
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.320
I just think it captures everything.
我只是觉得它捕捉到了一切。

62
00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:13.220
And you even have prison Mike on the computer screen.
而且你的电脑屏幕上甚至还有“监狱迈克”。

63
00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.720
So I'll share that in my stories.
所以我会在我的快拍里分享这个。

64
00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:20.240
But I just thought I had to give Max a thank you here on the podcast,
但我只是觉得我必须在这里的播客中向马克斯表达感谢，

65
00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.720
because that was so wonderful of him.
因为他真是太好了。

66
00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.440
Do you know about the artist that goes to thrift stores and buys paintings,
你知道那个去旧货店买画的艺术家吗，

67
00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.260
and then he paints people into them?
然后他在画里画上了人？

68
00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.600
Like he repurposes thrift art?
就像他改造旧货艺术品一样？

69
00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:40.920
Okay, so he took some thrifted painting of The Last Supper,
好吧，他拿了一幅旧货店买来的《最后的晚餐》的画，

70
00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.120
and he painted The Office into it.
然后他把《办公室》画了进去。

71
00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:48.060
So like on the table, there's like a stapler in Jell-O,
所以在桌子上，有像果冻里的订书机这样的东西，

72
00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.080
but then all of our characters are in the painting.
然后我们所有的角色都在画里面。

73
00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:55.460
And I saw his reel as he was doing it,
我看到他制作时的短视频了，

74
00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.040
and I made a comment where I said,
我留了个言说，

75
00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.560
oh, my gosh, I would love this.
噢，天哪，我太想要这个了。

76
00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:00.340
This is amazing.
这太棒了。

77
00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:04.400
And he, I guess, wrote me back and said, you can have it.
我猜他回信对我说，你可以拥有它。

78
00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:07.180
But I guess I didn't see his message in time,
但我想我没及时看到他的消息，

79
00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.860
and he ended up selling it.
结果他把它卖了。

80
00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:09.360
Aw.
啊。

81
00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:09.720
Bummer.
太遗憾了。

82
00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.760
But his stuff is really cool.
但他的作品真的很酷。

83
00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.620
It's really fun.
真的很有趣。

84
00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:18.060
This in nowhere is of the same magnitude of that really cool piece of art passing you by.
这绝对无法和那件你错过的超酷艺术品相提并论。

85
00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:18.720
Yes.
是的。

86
00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:24.080
But do you guys remember when I found out that there's a mustard wine by Grey Poupon?
但是你们还记得我发现灰 poupon 有一款芥末酒的时候吗？

87
00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:24.920
Yes.
记得。

88
00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.380
It's a long time ago for podcast listeners.
对播客听众来说是很久以前的事了。

89
00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:34.120
Well, I guess Grey Poupon reached out to us to send us their mustard wine,
好吧，我猜灰 poupon 联系我们说要给我们寄他们的芥末酒，

90
00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.380
and I never saw the DM.
而我从来没看到那条私信。

91
00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.460
And you missed it.
而你错过了。

92
00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.180
And now I can't find it.
现在我找不到了。

93
00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.960
I don't know where it's like buried in the DMs.
我不知道它被埋在私信的哪个地方。

94
00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.320
Jenna, that guy's name is Tyler Turnbull.
珍娜，那个家伙的名字叫泰勒·特恩布尔。

95
00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.300
Oh, thank you, Sam.
哦，谢谢你，萨姆。

96
00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:45.940
Tyler Turnbull.
泰勒·特恩布尔。

97
00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.180
Tyler Turnbull.
泰勒·特恩布尔。

98
00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:47.580
Okay.
好的。

99
00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:49.580
Well, we'll share about him in our stories.
我们会把他的情况分享到我们的快拍里。

100
00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:50.080
Yeah.
对。

101
00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.640
And I hope Grey Poupon reaches back out to you.
我也希望 Grey Poupon 能再次联系你。

102
00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:53.420
Yeah, Grey Poupon.
对，Grey Poupon。

103
00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:54.160
It's not too late.
现在还不算晚。

104
00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:54.480
Yeah.
对。

105
00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.540
Come back over.
回来吧。

106
00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.260
We'll try your mustard wine.
我们会试试你的芥末酒。

107
00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:01.720
Well, on this same subject, you know, after Lindsay Broad was on our podcast and she talked
说起这个，你知道的，在 Lindsay Broad 上了我们的播客之后，她谈到了

108
00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.840
about True Fru and how much she loves the chocolate-covered fruit from True Fru.
True Fru，以及她有多喜欢 True Fru 的巧克力包裹水果。

109
00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:06.380
Yeah.
对。

110
00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:09.940
They sent her a whole box of True Fru.
他们给她寄了一整箱 True Fru。

111
00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:10.900
That's awesome.
太棒了。

112
00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.180
She is so delighted.
她高兴极了。

113
00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.920
I was texting with her about it.
我正和她发短信聊这事呢。

114
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.080
She just texted me a photo of a giant box of True Fru, and I was like, what is happening?
她刚给我发了一张装着巨大一箱 True Fru 的照片，当时我就想，这是怎么回事？

115
00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.040
And how did this happen?
这事是怎么发生的？

116
00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:20.940
How did this occur?
怎么会这样？

117
00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:26.040
This is a really hard segue, but as you were saying that, all I could think of is like,
这个转折有点生硬，但当你说那些的时候，我脑子里唯一的想法就是，

118
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:29.580
there's got to be something, Cullen, you can take to help pass your kidney.
卡伦，肯定有什么东西是你吃了能帮排出肾结石的。

119
00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.220
Oh, no!
噢，不！

120
00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:32.480
Oh, no!
噢，不！

121
00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:33.040
Oh, no!
噢，不！

122
00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:36.800
Some sort of chocolate-covered fruit to help you pass her kidney stone?
某种巧克力包裹的水果能帮她排出肾结石？

123
00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:37.260
Yeah.
对。

124
00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:37.800
That's all I could think of.
我脑子里全是这个。

125
00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.180
I'm so sorry.
我太抱歉了。

126
00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.540
We're actually surprised you made it in today.
其实我们很惊讶你今天能来。

127
00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:45.900
I mean, Jenna and I have been texting you, and you shared with us, and you said it's okay
我是说，珍娜和我一直在给你发短信，你跟我们分享了，而且你说

128
00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:46.980
to talk about it.
可以聊这个。

129
00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:47.360
Yeah, absolutely.
对，完全可以。

130
00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:47.940
Yeah.
对。

131
00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.420
You have a kidney stone.
你长了肾结石。

132
00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:53.820
Yeah, we were meant to be meeting Monday, and I called in sick from urgent care.
对，我们本来打算周一开会，我在急诊中心请了病假。

133
00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:54.580
I know.
我知道。

134
00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:58.520
But I sent you an article, Cullen, and this is true.
但我给你发了一篇文章，卡伦，千真万确。

135
00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.400
Guys, this is not like internet nonsense.
伙计们，这不是网上那种瞎扯。

136
00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.240
Like, this isn't like some reel on the gram.
这可不是 Ins 上的那种短视频。

137
00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:10.960
This is a real article where they found that people with kidney stones, if they ride the
这是一篇真正的文章，上面发现有肾结石的人如果去坐

138
00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:16.240
roller coaster Big Thunder Mountain Railroad, they pass their kidney stones.
巨雷山铁路过山车，就能排出肾结石。

139
00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.080
Is it something about how it twists and turns?
是因为它那些七弯八绕的轨迹吗？

140
00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:19.840
Yes.
对。

141
00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:20.880
Yes.
对。

142
00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:21.860
It is.
就是这样。

143
00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:24.060
Colin, did you go to Disneyland yesterday?
科林，你昨天去迪士尼乐园了吗？

144
00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:24.940
I didn't.
我没去。

145
00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:27.620
I wondered if I could, like, claim it back on my health care, though.
不过我在想，我能不能把它当医疗费用报销呢。

146
00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.420
It seemed like it would be an excellent, like, deduction.
感觉这会是一笔绝佳的医疗抵扣。

147
00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:30.840
Yeah.
对。

148
00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.380
Medically speaking, you need to go.
从医学角度来讲，你得去一趟。

149
00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:33.020
Yeah.
对。

150
00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.540
Do you have an HSA card?
你有健康储蓄账户卡吗？

151
00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.080
Are you in pain?
你觉得痛吗？

152
00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:37.960
Anything even though?
虽然有什么不对劲吗？

153
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:38.680
Yeah, a little bit.
对，有一点。

154
00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:40.560
I just took some more painkillers.
我刚又吃了一些止痛药。

155
00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:41.700
I'm so sorry.
真的很抱歉。

156
00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:42.920
But it seems to, like, come and go.
但它好像是一阵一阵的。

157
00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:49.480
And it's particularly bad overnight because I'm one of those tornado sleepers that just
而且半夜特别严重，因为我是那种睡觉像龙卷风一样

158
00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.700
keeps spinning around.
转个不停的人。

159
00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:51.560
I'm like that too.
我也是这样。

160
00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:53.320
And really what I need to do is just lay still.
其实我真正需要做的是躺着别动。

161
00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.100
Oh, no.
噢，不是吧。

162
00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:59.600
You need to get a cat, and then the cat will sleep on you, and then you can't turn.
你需要养只猫，然后猫就会睡在你身上，这样你就动不了了。

163
00:05:59.600 --> 00:05:59.800
Okay.
好吧。

164
00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.340
Kessie, that's your answer to everything.
凯茜，你什么事都用这个答案。

165
00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:04.040
And that's deductible, right?
而且那个可以报销医疗费吧？

166
00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:04.440
Yeah.
对。

167
00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:07.900
Colin, I pulled up the article.
科林，我把那篇文章找出来了。

168
00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:12.660
I want everyone to know this information, and I really want to go to Disneyland with you.
我想让大家都知道这个信息，而且我真的很想跟你一起去迪士尼乐园。

169
